/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 489 0 R
/T (AGIS-based strategy aims to identify and rejuvenate dead and dying water sources, with objectives including the assessment of springs, prioritizing recharge areas, and community engagement in implementation. The project employs GIS technologies, remote sensing, and community involvement to develop a rejuvenation plan that includes mapping water sources and planning interventions. The rejuvenation plan provides micro-plans both mechanical treatments \(like infiltration holes, infiltration trenches, bio-plugs and check dams etc\) and biological treatments \(such as afforestation and nursery development etc\) to restore the watershed. Effective implementation of the rejuvenation measures requires collaborative efforts with local communities and government agencies to ensure sustainable practices. This plan emphasizes a phased approach to address the urgent needs of the local water  resources, beginning with the experimental areas of Jatha and Pass villages. Implementing these  measures will enhance groundwater availability, reduce land degradation, mitigate the process of adverse impacts of climate change and improve economic conditions for local inhabitants while promoting sustainable water management practices. )
/E (AGIS-based strategy aims to identify and rejuvenate dead and dying water sources, with objectives including the assessment of springs, prioritizing recharge areas, and community engagement in implementation. The project employs GIS technologies, remote sensing, and community involvement to develop a rejuvenation plan that includes mapping water sources and planning interventions. The rejuvenation plan provides micro-plans both mechanical treatments \(like infiltration holes, infiltration trenches, bio-plugs and check dams etc\) and biological treatments \(such as afforestation and nursery development etc\) to restore the watershed. Effective implementation of the rejuvenation measures requires collaborative efforts with local communities and government agencies to ensure sustainable practices. This plan emphasizes a phased approach to address the urgent needs of the local water  resources, beginning with the experimental areas of Jatha and Pass villages. Implementing these  measures will enhance groundwater availability, reduce land degradation, mitigate the process of adverse impacts of climate change and improve economic conditions for local inhabitants while promoting sustainable water management practices. )
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [5 6 7]
>>
endobj
