/T (1.1The Crucial Problem The Himalayan region, often referred to as the "Water Tower of Asia," is home to numerous rivers, springs, and naulas that support millions of people downstream. However,both the glacial fed and the rainfed river regimes of the Himalaya are facing an unprecedented crisis1-4. Springs, naulas and streams are drying up at an alarming rate, threatening the very fabric of rural livelihoods, agriculture, and ecosystems. The spatial distribution of rainfed rivers reveals that there are as many as 353 rain fed streams/rivers of more than fourth order, having a total length of about 5796km5. More than 45% of the geographical area of Uttarakhand is drained by non-glacial rain fed rivers wherein about more than 70% of villages more than 80% of urban centers are located.This rainfed rivers play a crucial role in supporting agriculture, industry, and human consumption in Uttarakhand.The major rainfed river systems of Uttarakhand are Kosi,Gaula,Saryu, western Ramganga,western and eastern Nayar etc. )
/E (1.1The Crucial Problem The Himalayan region, often referred to as the "Water Tower of Asia," is home to numerous rivers, springs, and naulas that support millions of people downstream. However,both the glacial fed and the rainfed river regimes of the Himalaya are facing an unprecedented crisis1-4. Springs, naulas and streams are drying up at an alarming rate, threatening the very fabric of rural livelihoods, agriculture, and ecosystems. The spatial distribution of rainfed rivers reveals that there are as many as 353 rain fed streams/rivers of more than fourth order, having a total length of about 5796km5. More than 45% of the geographical area of Uttarakhand is drained by non-glacial rain fed rivers wherein about more than 70% of villages more than 80% of urban centers are located.This rainfed rivers play a crucial role in supporting agriculture, industry, and human consumption in Uttarakhand.The major rainfed river systems of Uttarakhand are Kosi,Gaula,Saryu, western Ramganga,western and eastern Nayar etc. )
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [2 3]
>>
