<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 495 0 R
/E (Geologically, the rocks of the study area are composed of the Raut Gara Formation14 of the Damta Group \(Fig.3\) made-up of dominant quartzites often with feldspar and mica minerals; interbedded with fine grained foliated metamorphic phyllite with silky sheen; and fine-grained, low-grade metamorphic slate rocks15-16.These rocks have undergone significant tectonic activities, including metamorphism and thrust deformation, therefore are highly jointed and fractured and shared at places. )
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [7 8]
>>
