/T (The convex slopes are the recharge zones while the concave slope zones are discharge zones. The  convex slopes areas are the most suitable sites for mechanical treatment measures such as  infiltration holes and infiltration trenches for rainwater harvesting for groundwater augmentation.  This slope form is also suitable for contour trenching and terrace ponds. Wherever agricultural land  is available \(see Plate-XII and XII\). Wherever the agricultural and barren land is available on  concave slope, contour trenching and terrace ponds may be constructed for rainwater harvesting. )
/E (The convex slopes are the recharge zones while the concave slope zones are discharge zones. The  convex slopes areas are the most suitable sites for mechanical treatment measures such as  infiltration holes and infiltration trenches for rainwater harvesting for groundwater augmentation.  This slope form is also suitable for contour trenching and terrace ponds. Wherever agricultural land  is available \(see Plate-XII and XII\). Wherever the agricultural and barren land is available on  concave slope, contour trenching and terrace ponds may be constructed for rainwater harvesting. )
/Pg 25 0 R
/K [8 9]
>>
