989 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 513 0 R
/E (5.2.2.2 Plantation This is a process of establishing a forest plantation in an area often with a single species \(monoculture\). Typically, plantation involves non-native or commercial species for timber, pulp, or other products. This work may be done in association of the Forest Department. 5.2.2.3 Horticulture  It includes to development of community horticulture and individual horticulture programmers specially on the barren and abandoned agricultural lands in the recharge areas by which the waste land of the watershed could be carpeted by plants to increase rainwater infiltration capacity of land. This work should be done in association with the local inhabitants and the Department of Horticulture and Watershed Management.This will also improve the economic base of the local inhabitants. 5.2.2.4 Development of Nurseries It includes development of nurseries of broad-leaved plants, fruits, herbs and grasses etc.for conducting social forestry, community/individual horticultural and herbal gardening programmers in the recharge zones. This work should be done in association of the local community and the Department of Horticulture and forest. 5.2.2.5 Development of Horticulture/Floriculture For economic development of the area, development and horticulture and floriculture should also be started with the guidance of the department of horticulture and floriculture.Beside economic benefit these activities shall accelerate the process of rainwater infiltration and deaccelerate the process of erosion. )
/Pg 35 0 R
/K [2 3 4]
>>
endobj
990 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 513 0 R
/E (5.2.2.1 Afforestation Afforestation means establishing a forest in an area where there was no previous tree cover. This involves planting of native species, allowing natural regeneration, and promoting biodiversity.This may be done on degraded land, like barren areas or abandoned agricultural lands.It is suggested that in such available areas as the afforestation of water harvesting \(broad leaves\) species, local shrubs and grasses such as Napier and vertebrateshould be done by initiating massive social forestry programmed in the recharge areas with close association with local community and the Forest Department and Watershed Management Department. )
/Pg 35 0 R
/K [5 6]
>>
endobj
