/T (6.1.5 Contour Bunds The contour bunds are earthen embankments along contours to capture rainwater in agricultural land \(Plate-XII\). These help in storing the rainwater for infiltration to groundwater augmentation, reduce erosionand help in irrigating agricultural crops.These contour bunds should develop at the edge of agricultural land in association with the residents. As per rough estimate about 5000 running meters contour bunds shall be needed in the study area. Figure 14 depicts the notional locations of these contour bunds. )
